    "source_file_to_entries": {
        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "d716bcd5-791c-391c-9c29-ac79c6f78d18",
                "word": "inconsistency",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "6d3711be-b69e-4330-8686-e61a22e979d4",
                        "entry_id": "d716bcd5-791c-391c-9c29-ac79c6f78d18",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "inconsistencies"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "d12b7dcb-23cc-3a03-8c5f-4131a148f29a",
                        "entry_id": "d716bcd5-791c-391c-9c29-ac79c6f78d18",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The state of being inconsistent."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "996e1195-7f00-4ae4-a181-b6a2ffae22c7",
                                "sense_id": "d12b7dcb-23cc-3a03-8c5f-4131a148f29a",
                                "text": "It was a strange inconsistency, but never till then had I been so much struck with the worthless and frivolous life of society. Never till then did I feel the deep and eternal debt of gratitude that human nature owes to those who assert its higher influence; who feel their generous activity stirred by a thrice noble emulation; who appeal from the present to the future, and redeem their kind, by shewing of how much that is good and great ambition and genius are capable."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "1a68072a-421d-3ef7-82c9-ae4bc51be8df",
                        "entry_id": "d716bcd5-791c-391c-9c29-ac79c6f78d18",
                        "glosses": [
                            "An incompatibility between two propositions that cannot both be true."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "ab870e05-2ef6-4528-b72a-022ae7cb3101",
                        "source_entry_id": "d716bcd5-791c-391c-9c29-ac79c6f78d18",
                        "source_sense_description": "state of being inconsistent",
                        "target_lang_word": "inconsistentie",
                        "target_lang_code": "nl",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "inconsistentie",
                                "target_lang_code": "nl",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3d95bd6d-c49d-3d9d-8592-2a46709d23bb",
                                        "entry_id": "9225e5f3-eeda-3057-80d4-8271b7d63a60",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "gebrek aan samenhang, innerlijke tegenstrijdigheid"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a3615bc1-c2e1-44ac-8bf5-e901b27a1d98",
                                                "sense_id": "3d95bd6d-c49d-3d9d-8592-2a46709d23bb",
                                                "text": "Mensink: „Dat is een constante inconsistentie in veel onderzoek naar de publieke opinie. Veel mensen vinden dat er te veel vluchtelingen komen, maar voelen ook een morele plicht om vluchtelingen op te vangen. De grenzen volledig sluiten, gaat ze dan toch te ver.”"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "68a510d6-1a01-4dee-870b-b9215b12d8f3",
                                                "sense_id": "3d95bd6d-c49d-3d9d-8592-2a46709d23bb",
                                                "text": "Striplezers hechten zeer aan ‘continuïteit’ en dus moest er in de stripverhalen zelf een uitleg komen voor de inconsistenties."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4dbc01bc-98d2-4d09-a4bc-e4ee33b08d4d",
                                                "sense_id": "3d95bd6d-c49d-3d9d-8592-2a46709d23bb",
                                                "text": "⧖ Hij achtte het uitlokken van een Pauselijk verbod tegen staatkundige woelingen eene groote inconsistentie van de Britsche regering, die alle tijdelijk gezag aan den stoel van Rome betwistte."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "7315c5a6-4b78-40a3-98ae-7edaf56d4761",
                        "source_entry_id": "d716bcd5-791c-391c-9c29-ac79c6f78d18",
